# Presence of this file makes /etc/init.d/S02swap exit immediately: no zram, no
# SD swap, no VM sysctl changes. The board runs exactly as it did before the
# swap work landed.
#
# Shipped present because Stage 0 measured the board (2026-08-08, kernel
# 6.18.42, old image, app running) and the numbers do not justify swap:
#
#   OOM events, ever      0          <- docs/memory.md gates zram on this
#   AnonPages       8520 kB          <- the ENTIRE swappable working set
#   MemAvailable   23936 kB          <- healthy
#   allocstall_*         1  total    <- essentially no reclaim pressure
#   pgscan_direct       63  total
#   compact_stall        0
#   fastcarplay RssAnon 7192 kB      <- 84% of all anon memory
#
# A 24 MiB zram is ~3x the entire anonymous working set. Even swapping 100% of
# it at 2.5x compression nets ~5 MiB, and in practice far less because most of
# those 8.5 MiB are hot -- while costing CPU on the single 408 MHz core that is
# already the bottleneck for video decode.
#
# The real pressure on this board is CMA (CmaFree was 196 kB of 16384 kB at
# idle), and CMA is not swappable, so none of this would have helped it.
#
# The machinery is kept, tested and ready. To enable:
#
#   rm /etc/swap-disable && touch /etc/swap-sd && reboot     # zram + SD tier
#   rm /etc/swap-disable && reboot                           # zram only
#
# No rebuild needed for either -- p4 is already reserved on the card.
# Re-measure the numbers above before turning it on; if they still look like
# this, the answer is still no.
